# SRG-APP-000294-AU-000440  -  CAT III
# For devices and hosts within its scope of coverage, the Central Log Server
# must notify the System Administrator (SA) and Information System Security
# Officer (ISSO) when events indicating account removal actions are
# received.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000294-AU-000440
group:           V-206486
severity:        low
cat:             CAT III
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
revised:         yes
cci:             CCI-000015
control_rev5:    AC-2

contribution:    Splunk detects and sends the notification itself: a scheduled saved search
                 that mails the SA and ISSO when account-removal events are received, with
                 the relay and sender for the email action held in alert_actions.conf.

governs:         alert_actions.conf - What Splunk does when an alert fires, such as sending email or calling a
                 webhook.
governs:         savedsearches.conf - Saved searches, scheduled reports and alerts.

check:           savedsearches.conf [<search_name>] enableSched equals 1
check:           savedsearches.conf [<search_name>] cron_schedule non_empty
check:           savedsearches.conf [<search_name>] action.email matches ^(1|true)$
check:           savedsearches.conf [<search_name>] action.email.to non_empty
check:           alert_actions.conf [email] mailserver not_equals localhost
check:           alert_actions.conf [email] from matches ^[^@[:space:]]+@[^@[:space:]]+\.[A-Za-z]{2,}$
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
corrected:       alert_actions.conf [email] mailserver non_empty -> alert_actions.conf [email] mailserver not_equals localhost
corrected:       alert_actions.conf [email] from non_empty -> alert_actions.conf [email] from matches ^[^@[:space:]]+@[^@[:space:]]+\.[A-Za-z]{2,}$
vendor:          alert_actions.conf [email] from https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.3-configuration-file-reference/alert_actions.conf
vendor:          alert_actions.conf [email] mailserver https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.3-configuration-file-reference/alert_actions.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        The SMTP relay or mail gateway must accept and deliver the notification;
                 the specification states it is not included with the Splunk instance.
external:        The SA and ISSO mailbox addresses are organization-defined.
external:        Whether received events represent account-removal actions depends on the
                 sending hosts' audit configuration and on the source types parsing them.
external:        The SRG's own NA clause applies where notifications are performed by
                 another device.

citation:        The alert_condition condition is removed for the same reason as in
                 SRG-APP-000293-AU-000430: alert_condition defaults to an empty string and
                 is only one trigger form, counttype defaulting to "always" with relation
                 and quantity being the other (savedsearches.conf.spec:270-274, 249-253),
                 so requiring it non_empty reports a finding against a working alert and
                 against the plain scheduled report that the product STIG check for
                 SPLK-CL-000020 accepts ("verify that a report exists to notify the SA and
                 ISSO"). The remaining conditions are the send path the fix text names and
                 each tests a default that would otherwise not deliver: action.email
                 defaults to false (savedsearches.conf.spec:300-302), action.email.to is
                 REQUIRED and not defaulted (savedsearches.conf.spec:304-306), enableSched
                 defaults to 0 (savedsearches.conf.spec:73-77), mailserver defaults to
                 localhost against an SMTP server the product does not ship
                 (alert_actions.conf.spec:276-285), and from defaults to the bare word
                 "splunk" (alert_actions.conf.spec:163-165). This SRG also carries its own
                 NA clause.
finding:         Splunk Enterprise has no scheduled saved search that mails the SA and ISSO
                 when account-removal events are received: the search is not scheduled, the
                 email action or its recipient list is unset, or alert_actions.conf [email]
                 names no SMTP relay and no sender.
